  "uxGuardrails": [
    "Each interactive reel selects exactly one typed finite set with stable item IDs and a shown consequence.",
    "An off-screen or decorative paper crescent is noninteractive unless labeled and large enough to touch.",
    "Reel selection never applies wallpapers or activates an automation without explicit action.",
    "Return-to-grid preserves selected photo ID and ordering; large collections need search and jumping.",
    "Multiple reels only when separately typed selections are causally related and screen layout supports both.",
    "Home versus Lock paired reels are a design hypothesis, not an approved default.",
    "Any secondary reel collapses to a labeled selector before essential controls or large font text are compromised.",
    "Accessibility uses named prev/next and items; circular gestures never mandatory.",
    "Reel photo apertures must contain real image IDs, not filler repetitions implying false collection size."
  ],
